# thirdparty

This directory keeps RTL/software inputs used by the frontend flow. Heavy EDA
tools are intentionally not vendored here. Slang, Verilator, Yosys/OSS CAD
Suite, Surfer, and the RISC-V GCC toolchain should be installed through ECOS
Studio Resource Manager or supplied on `PATH`.

Quick tool check:

```bash
command -v slang
command -v verilator
command -v riscv32-unknown-elf-gcc || command -v riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc
command -v yosys
```

The CPU RTL release archive is trimmed to the source trees required by the
built-in adapter filelists, plus the corresponding license and notice files.
Large upstream test, example, verification, and generated-output trees remain
in the source submodules and are not part of the runtime resource package.
